  row (resp. vector along the last dimension).  Thus,

  >>> input = tf.random.normal(shape=(3,4,5,6))
  >>> k = 2
  >>> values, indices  = tf.math.top_k(input, k=k)
  >>> values.shape.as_list()
  [3, 4, 5, 2]
  >>>
